"The postoperative pathology revealed a Gleason 4+5 (ISUP grade group 5) and pathological stage pT3b. Adverse findings included positive surgical margins, invasion of the seminal vesicles, and lymphovascular invasion, although no lymph node metastasis was documented. The biopsy showed a Gleason 3+4 pattern with intraductal carcinoma and perineural invasion. These findings suggest a high-risk disease profile. Countervailing findings are limited as nodal status was documented, and the report states, \"there was no lymph node metastasis.\" The preoperative PSA was 7.8. Postoperative PSA is not recorded, meaning biochemical recurrence cannot be assessed. Missing postoperative PSA or follow-up information is critical for assessing the trajectory of the disease. Information regarding postoperative PSA and its subsequent trajectory would significantly revise the prognosis. The fixed estimated horizon is 29.84 months. This is a predicted recurrence horizon, not evidence of observed recurrence. The sensitivity range is 23.87–35.81 months; its coverage has not been validated."
